Adds **learn-omarchy**, an interactive Omarchy course with animated coaches,
spoken guidance, hands-on exercises, mixed practice, and printable shortcuts.
I'm the upstream author and will maintain this package.

- Repository: https://github.com/DanWahlin/learn-omarchy
- Release: @RELEASE_URL@
- Source archive: @SOURCE_URL@
- Source SHA-256: `@SHA256@`

### Packaging and updates

This is a source package, not a `-bin` repackaging. The release archive includes
the QML/JavaScript application, course material, recordings, artwork, and Omarchy
geometry companion. `make install` stages the payload without npm downloads,
cloud credentials, audio generation, or a separate companion package.

The recipe preserves the upstream package name `learn-omarchy`, so users of the
upstream Arch package can upgrade normally. `arch=('any')` describes the
architecture-independent payload, not a claim of desktop testing on every CPU.

Like #310, `.omarchy/package.json` requests the fast ring and a 24-hour release
quarantine. Unlike that binary package, this uses the upstream `SHA256SUMS`
manifest and one `any` source asset. Sync updates `pkgver` and the unsuffixed
`sha256sums`; stable `vX.Y.Z` tags map directly to Arch versions and asset names.
Drafts and prereleases are deliberately excluded.

### Dependencies and licensing

The PKGBUILD carries the upstream runtime dependencies and version floors for
Omarchy, Hyprland, Quickshell, Qt multimedia, Node.js, and the tools used by the
course. Optional OCR, QR, dictation, and activity-monitor tools remain optional.
The target is an Omarchy desktop, not vanilla Arch.

Code is MIT; original artwork and course content are CC BY 4.0; separately
identified recordings/example assets retain CC0-1.0. The archive contains the
notices and full license texts, and installs them under
`/usr/share/licenses/learn-omarchy`. A duplicate local LICENSE source is not needed.
There is no package install hook or privileged scan of users' home directories.
The launcher manages its bundled integration only for the user running the app;
package removal does not delete course progress.

### Validation to complete before submitting

- [ ] Record the clean Omarchy build and installed-payload verification results for @VERSION@.
- [ ] Link exact-release stable acceptance evidence, including fresh graphical install,
      offline use, upgrade/removal, attended activities, and supported display setups.
- [ ] Record the architectures actually tested; do not infer ARM desktop coverage from `any`.
- [ ] Validate metadata and release tracking against the current omarchy-pkgs checkout.
- [ ] Confirm the package name is still available and this package is not in the AUR.
- [ ] Obtain explicit approval to submit this PR.
